  "description": "A parametric MICROWAVE on the six-node spine — Geometry → Input Properties → Math Engine → Output Metrics → 2D Render + 3D Render.\n\nTHE CONTROL PANEL TAKES ITS WIDTH OFF THE DOOR, which is what a microwave actually looks like and what stops the two from overlapping when either is resized. Switch the panel off and the door runs the full width — a built-in with hidden controls.\n\nMOUNT CHANGES THE FRONT; the height is a separate number. A Countertop unit's door stands proud of the carcass; Built-in runs the carcass to full depth and recesses the door into it, because it lives in a housing; Over-range adds the vent strip a microwave doing a hood's job must have. \"Height above floor\" then puts any of the three at any level, so a microwave in a tall unit and one on a worktop are one object.\n\nCAVITY VOLUME at 55% of the carcass, because the cavity is not the case and the difference is the magnetron.",
